          "dimension": "current action and plan consistency",
          "fact": "DK wins the opening trick and preserves the resources needed by the retained plan.",
          "explanation": "The authorized trick is DQ–D3–D4, and South holds DAK. DK wins, leaving DA, HA and SA as controls. The unchanged CA–low club to CQ–C7 to CK route remains feasible with South CAK864 and North CQ72.",
          "quotes": [
            "Win with the king, then develop clubs immediately while retaining the diamond ace and both major-suit controls."
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
